d{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0f92926-0c15-554a-8fba-55b05d435980" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Least-Squares Regression Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78a1be33-b459-5e1d-a4ef-5ef29c50a8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375683} {:answer/id #uuid "7456bd36-2c63-5d55-a128-178ef9fb57ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375684} {:answer/id #uuid "53d11fdb-e71d-590e-8f5e-a7334512001e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}^{T}\\,(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375685} {:answer/id #uuid "d50dc6fe-95b3-5d96-be31-0b5c6ea95241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}X{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375686} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ffe801-4ed7-5b0c-ad48-3b9fca4c6f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X{X}^{T}\\,(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78a1be33-b459-5e1d-a4ef-5ef29c50a8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer